{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>Your woodcutters.</b> These are the male servants." "<b>Until your water drawers.</b> These are the female servants. And thus it is written: ״קטון וגדול שם הוא״. Another interpretation: קטון — this is David, as it is said: ״ודוד הוא הקטן״; and גדול — this is Moses, as it is said: ״והאיש משה גדול מאד״. Another interpretation: ״ועבד חפשי מאדוניו״ — these are Israel, for as long as a person is alive he is a servant to do the will of his Maker, and when he dies he becomes free from the commandments. Another interpretation: ״אתם נצבים היום כולכם״ — even though these curses come upon your enemies, you have enduring standing. Another interpretation: אתם נצבים — why did He make them a standing monument? Because they changed from loyalty to Him to loyalty to Joshua. And Joshua too made them a standing monument: ״ועתה התיצבו״, and ״ואשפטה אתכם לפני ה׳״. Another interpretation: When will they have standing and endurance — היום כולכם — when you are in one bond, all of you."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:01:31.161560672Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}